AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"rebar-debug bug 9f63: ROOT CAUSE proven — reconcile.py advanced its persisted events-log cursor to the newest event unconditionally at pass end, even when it had abandoned a candidate (check-error / review-timeout / voter error-or-deferred). ?t1= is a server-side inclusive lower bound (verified live), so an abandoned candidate left every future window permanently. Gerrit webhooks is at-MOST-once and the receiver queue is in-memory, so the reconciler is the ONLY recovery path — hence 'never voted until a human nudges it'. Both nudges work because each mints a fresh event AFTER the cursor. FIX: cursor is now a low-water mark min(newest, oldest retryably-abandoned), explicit terminal-vs-retryable partition, bounded hold-back via RECONCILE_MAX_HOLDBACK_SECONDS. Observability: /health gains queue_depth; reconcile_done gains held_back + cursor. Landed as Gerrit change 1512; LLM-Review +1 at 17:19:05 (17m58s after upload, auto-queued with NO manual nudge). Siblings filed: 6a65, b0f5. Worktree /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-dbg-9f63 branch dbg-9f63.","timestamp":1786124488609206001}],"created_at":1786124474879175001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f1edd0a0-0505-4bfe-aa12-5ff1449b0884","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9f63-16dc-f014-4df2"}],"description":"","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","9f63-16dc-f014-4df2"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"369b-171a-109a-49